crawshaw.io/sqlite v0.3.2 (ISC, see LICENSE), vendored as the SQLite binding in place of
database/sql and github.com/mattn/go-sqlite3, so queries prepare, bind, step and read columns
through SQLite's C API directly, as the reference (rusqlite) does.

Changes from upstream:

- c/sqlite3.c, sqlite3.h and sqlite3ext.h are SQLite 3.53.2, copied from the reference's
  libsqlite3-sys 0.38.2 (its sqlite3/ directory), so both applications run the same SQLite.
  3.53 includes 3.51.3's fix for the WAL-reset bug a checkpointer next to the writer could hit.
- The cgo CFLAGS in sqlite.go are libsqlite3-sys's "bundled" options (build.rs), plus
  SQLITE_ENABLE_UNLOCK_NOTIFY for blocking_step.c, compiled at -O3 as cargo's release profile does.
- wal.go adds NoteWALPages/TakeWALPages: a C WAL hook that records the WAL size after each
  commit, in place of the auto-checkpoint (internal/database runs checkpoints off the writer).
- row.c/row.h: Step reads the whole row in the same cgo call (campfire_step), and the column
  accessors answer from it when the column's type needs no conversion (otherwise they call SQLite,
  which converts). A room page reads about 750 values; read one cgo call at a time, the calls cost
  more than the reads. ColumnCount and BindParamCount are cached for the same reason.
- Removed: the sqlitex package, sessions, snapshots, blob I/O, user-defined functions,
  authorizers, extension loading and the incrementor, which Campfire doesn't use, with their
  C trampolines in wrappers.c, and the upstream tests that depended on them.
